From 80bf97362ab5f16078c96fc5b2ce01527088a2b6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dm1sh <me@dmitriy.icu>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 20:01:18 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Solve interactive Cloudflare challenges in a user-visible
 WebView

The headless WebView used by the Cloudflare interceptor immediately aborts
on challenges that need interaction (invisible WebView, no way to click).
Fall back to a small user-facing screen hosting the challenge WebView
after the headless attempt fails, so the person in front of the device
can complete interactive Turnstile challenges by hand.

The screen's WebView is loaded with the triggering request's headers -
most importantly its User-Agent - and shares the CF cookies with OkHttp
through the Android CookieManager, so the clearance earned by solving
here applies to the request that caused the challenge (including the
tracker API calls to domains like shikimori.rip).
